# Exploration (D-321): the landscape says where and how far, not the dice.

explore-not-from-here = one explores from a planet's ground: not from aboard and not from a room
explore-too-near = too close: the point is { $metres } m away, and from here one explores no nearer than { $near } m
explore-too-far = too far: the point is { $metres } m away, and from here one explores no farther than { $far } m
explore-not-land = there is water or the edge of the world there: a node has nothing to stand on
explore-into-water = the straight way there lies across water: from the shore one does not explore into the sea, a river is crossed at a ford
explore-no-room = it is crowded there: the ground is already taken — { $node }
explore-crosses-way = the way there would cross one already laid: one explores between ways, not across them
explore-already-out = a run is already under way
explore-run-dangling = job { $job }: the scout or the node it left from is gone
